INSERT INTO `longtexts` VALUES
('about_us','en','## Why this website?\n\nRoaddanger.org is firstly a database with traffic crashes. The purpose of this website is to gain insight how media are reporting on traffic crashes. Everybody can help by adding media articles about crashes to the database. Start by creating an account by clicking the profile button are the right top.\n\n## How to add a media article to this database?\n\n* Register yourself.\n* Click the + button in the top bar to add a new article.\n* Copy a media article link/url about a crash and paste it into the Link (url) field and click \"Fetch article\". Our spider will try to download most data. \n* Add the date of the crash (often different from the article date)\n* Add each of the involved humans separately and specify their transportation mode, injury and characteristics. These fields are important for our statistics.\n* Select \"Save and stay open\" to add multiple humans.\n* Adding the location is optional, but often hard to trace from the article.\n* A crash can only have one entry in our database, but you can add multiple articles to that crash. To add  another media article to a crash, select the about the same crash are grouped. To add another article to an existing crash select the crash options button (triple vertical dots ⋮ at the right top) and select \"Add article\".\n\n## When is a person \"injured\"?\n\nSomeone is injured if he or she is taken to an hospital by an ambulance.\n\n## Are the statistics you are showing accurate?\n\nNot really, but we are trying and you can help. The data is harvested from media articles. It becomes more accurate as more articles are added and we accurately tag the involved humans. However it will always just show rough trends. Location data is also hard quite to get accurately.\n\nWe remove duplicates, but that sometimes takes some time. Again, help us if you can.\n\n## Who is running this site?\n\nRoaddanger.org started as a spin-off from a journalistic project about traffic victims by journalist Thalia Verkade and  professor in Urban Mobility Futures Marco te Brömmelstroet on the online newspaper [De Correspondent](https://decorrespondent.nl/collectie/verkeersongevallen). The administrators of this website are journalist Thalia Verkade and programmer Jan Derk Stegeman.\n\n## I like to help or provide feedback\n\nIf you like to help add data, moderate, cooperate, program or just provide feedback you can email [Jan Derk Stegeman](mailto:info@digitaldutch.com). All code of this website is open source and available on [github](https://github.com/digitaldutch/roaddanger.org).\n\n## Cookies\nThis website only uses cookies to keep you logged in between sessions. That\'s all. However, the crash photographs are from the media websites who often place \"third-party\" cookies to track you.\n\n## Icons\n\nThe icons are created by [flaticon](https://www.flaticon.com/), [freepik](https://www.freepik.com/), [mavadee](https://www.flaticon.com/authors/mavadee), [monkik](https://www.flaticon.com/authors/monkik), [Online Web Fonts](https://www.onlinewebfonts.com/), [retinaicons](https://www.flaticon.com/authors/retinaicons) and [smalllikeart](https://www.flaticon.com/authors/smalllikeart).'),
('about_us','nl','## Wat is het doel van deze site?\n\nRoaddanger.org is in eerste plaats een database. Doel van deze site is meer inzicht te krijgen in hoe Nederlandse media schrijven over verkeersongevallen. Iedereen kan helpen om ongevallenberichtgeving te verzamelen: maak daarvoor een account aan via het profielmenu rechtsboven.\n\n## Hoe voeg ik een bericht aan deze database toe?\n\n* Registreer jezelf via het icoontje rechtsboven.\n* Kopieer een link/url van een bericht over een ongeval op een nieuwswebsite.\n* Log in of registreer en klik op het plus icoontje rechtsboven om een nieuw ongeval toe te voegen\n* Plak de url in het bovenste veld \"Artikel link (URL)\" en klik op \"Artikel ophalen\".\n* Vul de datum van het ongeval in (dit is niet per se de datum van het bericht), vul de betrokken voertuigen en het aantal doden en gewonden in. Als je met je muis boven de icoontjes zweeft, zie je een uitlegje van wat ze voorstellen. Kies eventuele andere kenmerken, zoals de betrokkenheid van kinderen.\n* Kies \"Opslaan en openblijven\" om meer voertuigen toe te voegen. Kies \"Opslaan en sluiten\" als je alle betrokken voertuigen hebt toegevoegd.\n* Meerdere berichten over één en hetzelfde ongeval plaatsen we bij elkaar. Om een bericht bij een al in de database opgenomen ongeval toe te voegen klik je op de drie bolletjes naast de icoontjes bij het ongeval en kies je: Artikel toevoegen.\n\n## Wie telt als \"gewond\"?\n\nWe tellen iemand als gewond als die als \"gewond\" wordt benoemd in een bericht of als een verkeersdeelnemer is afgevoerd met een ambulance / naar het ziekenhuis. We maken geen onderscheid tussen licht- en zwaargewonden.\n\n## Wat is \"dood\"?\n\nWe tellen de doden zoals die benoemd worden in de berichten.\n\n## Kloppen de cijfers met de werkelijkheid?\n\nDeze website is nadrukkelijk in aanbouw en op allerlei manieren onvolledig. De aandacht ligt bij de berichtgeving rondom verkeersongevallen en de taal die daarin gebruikt wordt.\n\nHet doel van deze site is niet volledigheid van cijfers, maar het krijgen van begrip over hoe we via media met elkaar praten over het verkeersleed in onze samenleving. De cijfers geven dus alleen een globaal beeld van wat er aan slachtoffers en verkeersdeelnemers in deze database te vinden is. Ook de locatiegegevens zijn vaak onnauwkeurig.\n\nWe weten zelf niet hoe volledig of onvolledig die berichtgeving is. Dubbeltellingen van ongevallen halen we eruit, maar dat gebeurt niet altijd meteen.\n\n## Wie beheren deze site?\n\nRoaddanger.org is begonnen als spin-off van het journalistieke project over verkeersongevallen van journalist Thalia Verkade en planoloog Marco te Brömmelstroet op [De Correspondent](https://decorrespondent.nl/collectie/verkeersongevallen). Beheerders zijn journalist Thalia Verkade en programmeur Jan Derk Stegeman.\n\n## Ik wil helpen modereren/samenwerken/de data gebruiken/de code uitbouwen of feedback geven, kan dat?\nFijn, stuur een mailtje naar [Jan Derk Stegeman](mailto:info@digitaldutch.com). Alle code van de deze website is open source en beschikbaar op [github](https://github.com/digitaldutch/roaddanger.org).\n\n## Cookies\nDeze website gebruikt een cookie om je ingelogd te houden tussen de verschillende pagina\'s. Verder niets. De foto\'s die getoond worden zijn echter van de nieuwswebsites en die plaatsen \"third-party\" cookies en kunnen je dus volgen.\n\n## Icoontjes\n\nIcoontjes zijn van [flaticon](https://www.flaticon.com/), [freepik](https://www.freepik.com/), [mavadee](https://www.flaticon.com/authors/mavadee), [monkik](https://www.flaticon.com/authors/monkik), [Online Web Fonts](https://www.onlinewebfonts.com/), [retinaicons](https://www.flaticon.com/authors/retinaicons) en [smalllikeart](https://www.flaticon.com/authors/smalllikeart).'),
('child_victims_info','de',''),
('child_victims_info','en','This live table shows child victims in traffic crashes. The data is inaccurate as it only shows child deaths from articles added to this website. It gets more accurate when more articles are added to this website. [How  can you help us?](/aboutthissite).'),
('child_victims_info','nl',''),
('counter_party_info','en','This live graph presents the transportation modes of the crash victims and their counterparties. A sort of \"who killed who\" generated from the data and articles added to this website. Click on a circle to show the crashes for that category.\n\nThe data is incomplete, but gets more accurate as more articles are added. [How  can you help us?](/aboutthissite)\n\n'),
('counter_party_info','nl','In deze live-tabel zie je welke partijen en tegenpartijen betrokken zijn bij verkeersongevallen die het nieuws haalden en op [deze website](/) zijn toegevoegd. \nJe kunt op de cijfers doorklikken om naar de nieuwsberichten te gaan.<br><br>\n\nDit is een onvolledige live grafiek die representatiever wordt naarmate er meer berichten worden toegevoegd. [Zo help je mee](/aboutthissite)'),
('questionnaires_answer','en','On this page, you can help our research project by answering questions about crashes that were in the news. For this particular project, we are interested in crashes with **2 parties** of all kinds of transportation modes. So, to fill in the questionnaire, use the **Humans filter** and select **2 parties**, each of **any transportation mode** (up to you). You can then answer questions for those types of crashes by clicking the first crash on the list, answering the questions, and clicking ‘next article’ to continue. '),
('questionnaires_answer','nl','Op deze pagina kun je ons helpen met ons onderzoeksproject door vragen te beantwoorden over ongevallen die in het nieuws zijn verschenen. Voor dit project zijn we geïnteresseerd in ongevallen met **2 partijen** met allerlei soorten vervoersmiddelen. Om de vragenlijst in te vullen, kun je dus het **Mensenfilter** gebruiken om **2 partijen** te selecteren, elk met **welk vervoersmiddel dan ook** (de keuze is aan jou). Vervolgens kun je vragen beantwoorden over deze soort ongevallen door te klikken op het eerste ongeval in de lijst, de vragen te beantwoorden en op \'next article\' te klikken om door te gaan. '),
('website_info','en','Traffic crashes kill and injure people worldwide on a massive scale. This doesn’t happen ‘by accident’; it’s a consequence of the political choice to design our public spaces for fast and efficient movement from A to B. However, as a society, we seem not to view traffic crashes as a major social issue and a human tragedy, and we rarely address the systemic causes. This is partly sustained by the limited journalistic coverage of traffic crashes. The human suffering is barely described; we often talk about vehicles rather than people (‘van hits car’), and traffic crashes are seen as ‘accidents’ rather than the result of political policy.\n\nWith this website, we want to show how the media report on traffic crashes and initiate a change. We collect news articles and data on framing. To make this data as complete and representative as possible, we need your help. All website visitors can contribute by adding a news report and answering a few short questions about the framing. Click [here](https://nl.roaddanger.org/aboutthissite/) for an explanation.\n\nIf we raise enough awareness together, we can help ensure that a safe, peaceful, and social public space becomes a priority again, and that traffic victims are once more seen as people.\n\nMore (scientific) background information on the causes and framing of traffic accidents:\n\n[Scientific article](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2590198220300208?via%3Dihub) ‘Framing systemic traffic violence’ by Prof. Dr. Marco te Brömmelstroet\n\n[Column (in Dutch)](https://decorrespondent.nl/11231/onze-straten-zijn-zo-ingericht-dat-er-in-een-week-vijf-kinderen-konden-omkomen-dat-is-een-keuze/1180906799325-3d2f0785) ‘Our streets are designed in a way that allowed five children to die in a week. That is a choice’ by Thalia Verkade\n\n[Journalistic article (in Dutch)](https://decorrespondent.nl/9272/busje-ramt-auto-file-na-ongeluk-en-de-mensen-dan/974923679400-3cc81f84) ‘Van hits car, traffic jam after accident. And what about the people?’ by Thalia Verkade'),
('website_info','nl','Verkeersongevallen doden en verwonden mensen wereldwijd op massale schaal. Dit gebeurt niet \'per ongeluk\', maar als gevolg van de politieke keuze om onze openbare ruimte in te richten voor snelle en efficiënte verplaatsing van A naar B. Maar als samenleving lijken we verkeersongevallen niet te zien als een groot maatschappelijk probleem en een menselijk drama. En we pakken de systemische oorzaken nog amper aan. Dit wordt deels in stand gehouden door de beperkte journalistieke verslaggeving over verkeersongevallen. Het menselijk leed wordt nauwelijks beschreven, we spreken vaak over voertuigen in plaats van mensen (‘busje ramt auto’) en verkeersongevallen zijn een ‘ongeluk’ in plaats van het gevolg van politiek beleid. \n\nMet deze website willen we aan Nederland laten zien hoe de media over verkeersongevallen schrijven en een verandering in gang zetten. We verzamelen nieuwsberichten en data over de framing. Om die data zo compleet en representatief mogelijk te maken, hebben we jouw hulp hard nodig. Alle bezoekers van de website kunnen meehelpen door een nieuwsbericht toe te voegen en een paar korte vragen te beantwoorden over de framing. Klik [hier](https://nl.roaddanger.org/aboutthissite/) voor uitleg. \n\nAls we hier samen genoeg bewustzijn over verspreiden, kunnen we ervoor zorgen dat een veilige, vredige en sociale openbare ruimte weer prioriteit wordt, en dat verkeersslachtoffers weer als mensen worden gezien. \n\nMeer (wetenschappelijke) achtergrondinformatie over de oorzaken en framing van verkeersongevallen:\n\n[Wetenschappelijk artikel](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2590198220300208?via%3Dihub) \'Framing systemic traffic violence\' van prof. dr. Marco te Brömmelstroet\n\n[Column](https://decorrespondent.nl/11231/onze-straten-zijn-zo-ingericht-dat-er-in-een-week-vijf-kinderen-konden-omkomen-dat-is-een-keuze/1180906799325-3d2f0785) \'Onze straten zijn zo ingericht dat er in een week vijf kinderen konden omkomen. Dat is een keuze\' van Thalia Verkade\n\n[Journalistiek artikel](https://decorrespondent.nl/9272/busje-ramt-auto-file-na-ongeluk-en-de-mensen-dan/974923679400-3cc81f84) ‘Busje ramt auto’, ‘file na ongeluk’. En de mensen dan?\' van Thalia Verkade');
INSERT INTO `ai_models` VALUES
('deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro','DeepSeek: DeepSeek V4 Pro','DeepSeek V4 Pro is a large-scale Mixture-of-Experts model from DeepSeek with 1.6T total parameters and 49B activated parameters, supporting a 1M-token context window. It is designed for advanced reasoning, coding,...',1048576,'2026-04-24',0.00000044,0.00000087,1),
('google/gemini-3-flash-preview','Google: Gemini 3 Flash Preview','Gemini 3 Flash Preview is a high speed, high value thinking model designed for agentic workflows, multi turn chat, and coding assistance. It delivers near Pro level reasoning and tool use performance with substantially lower latency than larger Gemini variants, making it well suited for interactive development, long running agent loops, and collaborative coding tasks. Compared to Gemini 2.5 Flash, it provides broad quality improvements across reasoning, multimodal understanding, and reliability.\n\nThe model supports a 1M token context window and multimodal inputs including text, images, audio, video, and PDFs, with text output. It includes configurable reasoning via thinking levels (minimal, low, medium, high), structured output, tool use, and automatic context caching. Gemini 3 Flash Preview is optimized for users who want strong reasoning and agentic behavior without the cost or latency of full scale frontier models.',1048576,'2025-12-17',0.00000050,0.00000300,1),
('inception/mercury-2','Inception: Mercury 2','Mercury 2 is an extremely fast reasoning LLM, and the first reasoning diffusion LLM (dLLM).\nInstead of generating tokens sequentially, Mercury 2 produces and refines multiple tokens in parallel, achieving >1,000 tokens/sec on standard GPUs. Mercury 2 is 5x+ faster than leading speed-optimized LLMs like Claude 4.5 Haiku and GPT 5 Mini, at a fraction of the cost. \nMercury 2 supports tunable reasoning levels, 128K context, native tool use, and schema-aligned JSON output. Built for coding workflows where latency compounds, real-time voice/search, and agent loops. OpenAI API compatible. Read more in the [blog post](https://www.inceptionlabs.ai/blog/introducing-mercury-2).',128000,'2026-03-04',0.00000025,0.00000075,1),
('mistralai/mistral-large-2512','Mistral: Mistral Large 3 2512','Mistral Large 3 2512 is Mistral’s most capable model to date, featuring a sparse mixture-of-experts architecture with 41B active parameters (675B total), and released under the Apache 2.0 license.',262144,'2025-12-01',0.00000050,0.00000150,1),
('mistralai/mistral-small-2603','Mistral: Mistral Small 4','Mistral Small 4 is the next major release in the Mistral Small family, unifying the capabilities of several flagship Mistral models into a single system. It combines strong reasoning from...',262144,'2026-03-16',0.00000015,0.00000060,1),
('openai/gpt-4.1','OpenAI: GPT-4.1','GPT-4.1 is a flagship large language model optimized for advanced instruction following, real-world software engineering, and long-context reasoning. It supports a 1 million token context window and outperforms GPT-4o and GPT-4.5 across coding (54.6% SWE-bench Verified), instruction compliance (87.4% IFEval), and multimodal understanding benchmarks. It is tuned for precise code diffs, agent reliability, and high recall in large document contexts, making it ideal for agents, IDE tooling, and enterprise knowledge retrieval.',1047576,'2025-04-14',0.00000200,0.00000800,1);
INSERT INTO `ai_prompts` VALUES
(2,1,NULL,'google/gemini-3-flash-preview','Where did Apollo 11 land?','','',NULL),
(13,1,'article_analyst','openai/gpt-4.1','Article date: [article_date]\nArticle title: [article_title]\nArticle text: [article_text]','You are a research data analyst of media articles about crashes. Get the location of the crash, the transportation modes involved and for each transportation mode the humans involved. For the involved humans get a description and health status and other properties.','{\"type\":\"json_schema\",\"json_schema\":{\"name\":\"crash_data\",\"strict\":true,\"schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"language\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"pattern\":\"^[a-z]{2}$\",\"description\":\"Language code using ISO 639-1 alpha-2 format (two lowercase letters)\"},\"crash_date\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"date\",\"description\":\"Date of the crash in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD)..\"},\"single_party_incident\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"True if the incident involved only one party (vehicle, cyclist, pedestrian, train, etc.) without collision with or involvement of any other parties\"},\"animals_mentioned\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"True if animals of any kind (pets, wildlife, livestock) were mentioned in relation to the crash, regardless of their role\"},\"traffic_congestion\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Indicates whether the incident caused traffic congestion, road closures, or significant delays\"},\"location\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"description\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Specific location of the incident, formatted as street address, intersection, or landmark with sufficient detail to pinpoint on a map. Add city and country.\"},\"geocoder_prompt\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Create a prompt for geocoders: Specific location of the incident, formatted for geocoding. Add street, city and country. If the location is an intersection, provide the street names in the format \'street name 1 & street name 2\'\"},\"coordinates\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"latitude\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"longitude\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"latitude\",\"longitude\"],\"additionalProperties\":false},\"country_code\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"pattern\":\"^[A-Z]{2}$\",\"description\":\"Country code using ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 format (two uppercase letters)\"}},\"required\":[\"description\",\"geocoder_prompt\",\"coordinates\",\"country_code\"],\"additionalProperties\":false},\"transportation_modes\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"description\":\"List all transportation modes involved in the crash separately. For example, instead of grouping similar modes (e.g., \'2 cars\'), each instance should be listed individually (e.g., \'car 1\', \'car 2\', \'bike\', etc.).\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"transportation_mode\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Select the closest mode. A fatbike categorizes as a bicycle. The Dutch word scooter means motorscooter.\",\"enum\":[\"unknown\",\"pedestrian\",\"bicycle\",\"motorScooter\",\"motorcycle\",\"car\",\"taxi\",\"emergencyVehicle\",\"deliveryVan\",\"tractor\",\"bus\",\"tram\",\"truck\",\"train\",\"wheelchair\",\"mopedCar\",\"scooter\"]},\"description\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"humans\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"description\":\"List all humans in a transportation mode separately. Instead of grouping humans (e.g. 2 persons) list them als human 1 and human 2. For transportation modes that require human operation (cars, bicycles, motorcycles, etc.) but don\'t explicitly mention humans, assume 1 human operator and add them to the list.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"description\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"health\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"dead\",\"injured\",\"uninjured\",\"unknown\"]},\"intoxicated\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"child\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"fled_scene\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"}},\"required\":[\"description\",\"health\",\"intoxicated\",\"child\",\"fled_scene\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},\"required\":[\"transportation_mode\",\"description\",\"humans\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},\"required\":[\"language\",\"crash_date\",\"single_party_incident\",\"animals_mentioned\",\"traffic_congestion\",\"location\",\"transportation_modes\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}}',24322),
(14,1,'translator','mistralai/mistral-large-2512','[article_text]','You are a translator to English. Output only the English translation.\n\nTranslate literally, do not add, omit, or interpret. Preserve all facts, numbers, tenses, and attributions exactly. No summarizing, no paraphrasing, no smoothing.','',21878),
(15,1,'article_reframe_UVA','mistralai/mistral-large-2512','Article title: \n[article_title]\n\nArticle text:\n[article_text]','You are a journalism expert specializing in traffic crash reporting.\n\nYour task is to:\n1. Determine whether the article is about a traffic crash (e.g., car crash, pedestrian hit, bicycle accident).\n2. Analyze the headline against three humanization criteria.\n3. If it\'s a crash article, rewrite the headline to better meet all three criteria.\n\nCriteria Definitions:\n\nCriteria Id 1: Headline mentions all parties\nThis is Yes if:\n- All parties mentioned in the article body as being involved in the crash are also mentioned in the headline\n- A party can be mentioned either by referring to the person (e.g., \"woman\", \"driver\") or their vehicle (e.g., \"car\", \"truck\")\n- For single-party crashes (e.g., vehicle ran off road), Yes if that party is mentioned\n- A party is always a human. Trees or other objects don\'t count\n\nCriteria Id 2: Headline uses human terms\nThis is Yes if ALL parties in the headline are described using:\n• Human terms (e.g., \"woman,\" \"man,\" \"child,\" \"person,\" \"teenager\")\n• Role-based terms (e.g., \"driver,\" \"pedestrian,\" \"cyclist,\" \"passenger\")\n• Quantified human references (e.g., \"one person\", \"two people\", \"three victims\")\n\nThis is No if ANY party in the headline is described as:\n• A transportation mode (e.g., \"car,\" \"bicycle,\" \"truck,\" \"vehicle\") instead of the person operating it\n• Dehumanizing statistics without human context (e.g., \"1 killed,\" \"2 injured,\" \"fatality\")\n• Numbers alone to represent humans (e.g., \"1 dead in crash\")\n\nCriteria Id 3: ACTIVE VOICE:\nThis is Yes if:\n• The headline uses active voice to clearly show who/what performed the action\n\nThis is No if:\n• The headline uses passive constructions that obscure agency (e.g., \"was struck,\" \"was hit,\" \"killed in crash\", \"dies\")\n• Outcome-only descriptions without clear agency (e.g., \"Person killed in crash,\" \"X injured\")\n    \nExamples for scoring headlines against the criteria:\n\nHeadline: \"Bicyclist injured after crash on Granny White Pike in Brentwood\"\nAnalysis:\n1. MENTION ALL PARTIES: No - Only mentions bicyclist, missing the other party (driver/vehicle)\n2. USE HUMAN TERMS: Yes - Uses \"bicyclist\" which is a human role term \n3. ACTIVE VOICE: No - Uses passive \"injured after\" instead of showing who performed the action\n\nHeadline: \"Pedestrian struck and killed by car on Old Hickory Boulevard\"\nAnalysis:\n1. MENTION ALL PARTIES: Yes - Mentions both pedestrian and car, all parties involved\n2. USE HUMAN TERMS: No - Uses \"car\" instead of \"driver\"\n3. ACTIVE VOICE: No - Uses passive \"struck and killed\" instead of showing the driver\'s action\n\nHeadline: \"Driver of truck strikes and kills pedestrian in New York City\"\nAnalysis:\n1. MENTION ALL PARTIES: Yes - Mentions both driver and the pedestrian\n2. USE HUMAN TERMS: Yes - Uses \"driver\" and \"pedestrian\" (both human role terms)\n3. ACTIVE VOICE: Yes - \"Driver strikes and kills\" clearly shows who performed the action\n\nNext, please rewrite the headline to ensure it:\n1. Mentions all parties involved in the crash \n2. Uses human terms instead of transportation modes to refer to all parties\n3. Uses active voice that clearly shows who did what to whom\n\nThe rewritten headline should:\n- Be in similar style to the original headline\n- Be appropriate for a news article\n- Be concise and clear\n- Not assign blame to victims and beyond what is factually stated in the article\n- Avoid naming specific car models or brands and be respectful of the victims\n- Focus on human impact rather than traffic disruption\n\nThe rewritten headline should be in the same language as the original headline (e.g. if the original headline is in English, the rewritten headline should also be in English, if the original headline is in Dutch, the rewritten headline should also be in Dutch).\n\nExamples for Rewriting Headlines:\n\nOriginal: \"Two adults suffer serious injuries from I-70 collision\"\nRewritten: \"Driver causes collision on I-70, injuring two adults\"\nKey changes made: The revised headline now references the missing party (driver) and uses active voice \"causes collision, injuring\" instead of passive \"suffer serious injuries\".\n\nOriginal: \"Pedestrian struck and killed by car on Old Hickory Boulevard\"\nRewritten: \"Driver of car strikes and kills 21-year-old man on Old Hickory Boulevard\"\nKey changes made: The revised headline uses human terms (\"driver\" instead of \"car\") and active voice (\"strikes and kills\") instead of passive (\"struck and killed\")\n','{\n  \"type\": \"json_schema\",\n  \"json_schema\": {\n    \"name\": \"analysis\",\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"schema\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"isRelevant\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"description\": \"True if article is about a crash\"\n        },\n        \"improvedHeadline\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Rewritten headline according system prompt\"\n        },\n        \"criteriaResults\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"description\": \"\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"criterionId\": {\n                \"type\": \"integer\",\n                \"description\": \"The ID of the criteria\"\n              },\n              \"passed\": {\n                \"type\": \"boolean\"\n              },\n              \"explanation\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\"criterionId\", \"passed\", \"explanation\"],\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n          }\n        },\n        \"changes\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"description\": \"What you did to make the rewritten headline fullfill the criteria. Leave the explanation field empty if the original already fullfilled the criteria\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"criterionId\": {\n                \"type\": \"integer\",\n                \"description\": \"The ID of the criteria\"\n              },\n              \"explanation\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"description\": \"What you changed to fullfill the criteria\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\"criterionId\", \"explanation\"],\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"isRelevant\", \"improvedHeadline\", \"criteriaResults\", \"changes\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    }\n  }\n}\n',21853),
(16,1,'article_reframe','mistralai/mistral-large-2512','Article title: \n[article_title]\n\nArticle text:\n[article_text]','You are a journalist assistant specializing in rewriting crash reports (title and full text) to make them more humane, respectful, and accurate.\n\nAlways mention people, not their mode of transport. Replace phrases like “the car hits bike” with “the car driver hit the cyclist.” \n\nMention the people involved: If the original article omits who was hurt or killed, add general terms like “a cyclist,” “a pedestrian,” or “a person in the other car” to humanize them. If the person’s role is unclear, use respectful, neutral wording.\n\nAvoid passive voice when it hides agency: Instead of “Cyclist was hit by a truck” prefer “A truck driver hit a cyclist”.\n\nRespect the dignity of those affected: Never sensationalize. Avoid phrases that distance or minimize human harm, like “the vehicle was totaled” if people were injured or killed.\n\nClarify known facts, acknowledge unknowns: If it\'s unclear who caused the crash, avoid assumptions, but don\'t erase agency by treating the crash like a natural disaster.\n\nOptional: Where appropriate, add a closing sentence that recognizes the impact on the community or the need for safer infrastructure.\n\nRespond in the same language as the article.','{\n    \"type\": \"json_schema\",\n    \"json_schema\": {\n        \"name\": \"crash_data\",\n        \"strict\": true,\n        \"schema\": {\n\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n                \"title\": {\n                    \"type\": \"string\",\n                    \"description\": \"The title or headline of the article.\"\n                },\n                \"text\": {\n                    \"type\": \"string\",\n                    \"description\": \"The full body of the article, including all paragraphs.\"\n                }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\"title\", \"text\"],\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n        }\n    }\n}\n',21865),
(23,1,'questionnaire_answerer','inception/mercury-2','Article title: [article_title]\nArticle text: [article_text]\n\nQuestionnaires:\n[questionnaires]\n\n','You are a research analyst AI that evaluates news articles using a fixed questionnaire.\n\nYou will receive:\nThe article title\nThe full article text\nA list of numbered questions that must be answered in order\n\nYour task:\nRead the headline and article carefully. Answer the questions strictly in the given order.\nFor each question, output only: yes, no or \'not_determinable\'. The last one if the question cannot clearly be answered by either yes or no. \n\nFollowed by a short, precise justification (max 150 characters), explicitly referring to the article text.\n\nThere are two types of questionnaires: \'bechdel\' and \'standard\'.\n\nFor standard type questionnaires just answer all questions.\n\nFor Bechdel type questionnaires: \nAs soon as any question is answered with \'no\' or \'not determinable\', immediately stop and do not answer any further questions. Do not skip questions. Do not reorder questions. Do not add commentary outside the answers. Do not assume information that is not explicitly stated in the article.\n\nOutput format example:\n\nyes – The headline explicitly names both drivers involved.\nno – The subject is a vehicle rather than a human actor.\n(Stop here because a \"No\" was given.)\n\nAnswer in English. Be objective, literal, and conservative: if something is ambiguous or implied rather than explicit, answer No.','{\"type\":\"json_schema\",\"json_schema\":{\"name\":\"crash_data\",\"strict\":true,\"schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"questionnaires\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"id\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"type\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"standard\",\"bechdel\"]},\"questions\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"id\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"answer\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"yes\",\"no\",\"not_determinable\"]},\"justification\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"maxLength\":150}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"answer\",\"justification\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"type\",\"questions\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},\"required\":[\"questionnaires\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}}',25213);
